      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have been thinking about it.  The names of pins are of the form `CNxx_xx` meaning that even if a we do gpio monitoring of the maximum of 16 pins it would use 128 characters worst case, leaving another 128 for the rest of the parameters on the command line.  I do not think that we will run into issues with a 256 character limit.\n\nAlso, the EC code by default reserves space for a command history of length 8, so any increase will be multiplied.  We do have the RAM, but I think it also makes sense to save some for future uses, since I doubt there is any benefit from going above 256.",
